    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d77">

                <pb facs="0221" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v12/pg181"/>

                <head>77. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Turkey<anchor n="1" xml:id="d77-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-11-02T16:40:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                                1955—4:40 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>801. Department informed Turk Ambassador November 1 US will not advise against
                    Jordanian adherence Baghdad Pact and if Jordan asks our views we will state we
                    consider Pact useful instrument in <pb facs="0222" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/>
                    development collective security for Middle East area and that we continue fully
                    support it. However we pointed out that if Jordan adhered prior to settlement
                    Jordan-Israeli boundary this would create an additional difficulty in connection
                    with possible US adherence and that our purpose is to seek agreement on
                    boundaries.</p>
                <p>Turk Ambassador expressed appreciation for forthcoming US attitude which he
                    characterized as “important step forward”. He was concerned however over
                    possibility that Jordanian adherence might make US adherence less likely. He was
                    informed that US adherence not immediately foreseeable in any event and we saw
                    no reason why Turkish President should not sound out situation in Amman.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Hoover</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d77-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d77-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 780.5/11–255. Secret; Priority.
                    Drafted by Kitchen and
                        Allen who approved and signed for Hoover. Repeated to London, Amman, and Geneva
                    for Secretary Dulles.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
